From 194893b44730b2173469aa798e08f4e62851f0e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 23:53:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(quick-match): cricket innings transitions as a
 post-commit effect + break screen (#106)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Innings flip and match-finish ran as side effects INSIDE the setScores updaters
(addRuns/addWicket/addExtra), so they read stale closure state and could double-
fire when React re-invokes an updater (StrictMode/batching) — risking a double
finalize. Make the updaters pure and move all transitions to ONE post-commit
effect that reads committed state.

Ordering is preserved: the boundary ball's broadcast is gated on a one-shot intent
ref, so the innings/battingTeam change re-runs that effect harmlessly (no new
intent -> no spurious feed event); and finishCricketMatch defers setPhase('result')
to the next render, so the winning ball still enqueues before finalize drains (R1).

Also adds the cricket innings-break interstitial (item 9): an innings-1 summary +
chase target shown before innings 2, dismissed with "Start innings 2". Not
persisted, so a reload simply resumes scoring; reset on a new match.

Tests (StrictMode) assert exactly one innings flip with no premature finalize, and
exactly one persist/finalize when the second innings ends — the regression a
double-invoked updater would have produced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
